# Google Cloud Storage

## Gate

Use when the user asks about GCS buckets, objects, lifecycle, or bucket IAM.
Prefer `gcloud storage` (or `gsutil` when already the local habit). Skip when
the ask is only Compute/GKE with no bucket named.

## Transport

No Google Cloud MCP discovered. Use `gcloud storage` / `gsutil`. Prefer a
Cloud MCP later if ready — do not invent tool names.

## Resolve ids

Never invent bucket or object names. Resolve from the user or a list:

| Need | Command |
| --- | --- |
| List buckets | `gcloud storage buckets list --project=PROJECT` |
| Describe bucket | `gcloud storage buckets describe gs://BUCKET` |
| List objects (prefix) | `gcloud storage ls gs://BUCKET/PREFIX` |
| Object metadata | `gcloud storage objects describe gs://BUCKET/OBJECT` |
| Bucket IAM get | `gcloud storage buckets get-iam-policy gs://BUCKET` |

Prefer metadata and short prefix listings over dumping object bodies into
chat. Cap listings with prefixes / `--recursive` only when asked.

## Read vs body

1. Metadata-first: name, location, storage class, versioning, uniform
   bucket-level access.
2. Downloads: follow the user’s named local path
   (`gcloud storage cp gs://… ./path`). Do not paste binaries or large
   payloads into chat.
3. Text peek: only small, non-secret objects the user named; redact
   credentials if they appear.

## Write / copy (gated)

Uploads, copies, and lifecycle edits need an explicit verb naming the
bucket/object:

| Action | Command shape |
| --- | --- |
| Upload | `gcloud storage cp LOCAL gs://BUCKET/OBJECT` |
| Copy | `gcloud storage cp gs://SRC gs://DST` |
| Lifecycle / class | `gcloud storage buckets update …` — only named fields |

## Public ACL and IAM (high risk)

Making a bucket or object public, or granting `allUsers` /
`allAuthenticatedUsers`, needs an **explicit** public/share verb this turn.
Prefer uniform bucket-level access + narrow principals. Follow
`google-cloud-safety`.

Do not print full IAM policy dumps with every member when a short answer
suffices (bucket + role + principal count / named principal).

## Defaults

1. Always include `gs://bucket` (and object) in receipts.
2. Prefer project-scoped bucket lists before mutating.
3. Soft-delete / versioning: mention retention implications before delete.
4. Signed URLs: only when asked; never paste long-lived credentials.

## Refuse

- Public ACL / `allUsers` without an explicit public verb.
- Delete buckets/objects without `google-cloud-safety` and a clear delete
  ask naming each target.
- Inventing bucket names or assuming a prod bucket from a short alias.
- Committing GCS HMAC keys or service-account keys into the repo or chat.
